/-!
# The resolvent of a strongly continuous contraction semigroup

For a strongly continuous contraction semigroup `S` on a real Banach space and a positive shift
`μ`, the resolvent is the Laplace transform of the orbits,

  `S.resolvent μ x = ∫₀^∞ e^{-μ t} S t x dt`,

a bounded operator of norm at most `μ⁻¹` (`opNorm_resolvent_le`).  The resolvent inverts `μ − L`
on the generator domain, `R_μ (μ f − L f) = f` (`resolvent_smul_sub_generator`, by the product
rule and the fundamental theorem of calculus on `[0, ∞)`), and `μ − L` inverts it on the whole
space: `R_μ x` lies in the domain with `L (R_μ x) = μ R_μ x − x` (`resolvent_mem_generatorDomain`,
`generator_resolvent`).  The latter is proved first for `x` in the domain, where `R_μ` commutes
with the difference quotients, and extended to all `x` by density of the domain and closedness of
the generator (`Semigroup/GeneratorClosed.lean`).

Consequently the domain is the range of every resolvent (`generatorDomain_eq_range_resolvent`),
the resolvents satisfy the resolvent identity (`resolvent_sub_resolvent`) and have dense range
(`denseRange_resolvent`), so they form a contractive resolvent in the sense of
`Semigroup/ContractiveResolvent.lean` (`toContractiveResolvent`).  That the semigroup generated by
this contractive resolvent is `S` itself is proved in `Semigroup/ResolventGeneration.lean`.

Main results: `laplaceIntegrand` and its integrability, `resolvent`, `resolvent_apply`,
`opNorm_resolvent_le`, `operator_resolvent`, `resolvent_smul_sub_generator`,
`resolvent_mem_generatorDomain`, `generator_resolvent`, `generator_eq_of_resolvent_eq`,
`generatorDomain_eq_range_resolvent`, `resolvent_sub_resolvent`, `denseRange_resolvent`,
`toContractiveResolvent`.

The shift `μ` is a positive real; nothing is asserted for complex shifts or for the spectrum of the
generator beyond the half-line `(0, ∞)`.
-/

